infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Per-request DataLoader vs a global singleton
  desc Same loader, opposite safety — a global instance is a cache shared across every request
  compares
    - label Per-request instance
      children
        - label Fresh cache every request
          desc New DataLoader built in the context factory, GC'd when the request ends
        - label Tenant isolation
          desc No request can read another tenant's cached row for the same ID
        - label Always current
          desc A row updated mid-flight is re-fetched, never served stale
    - label Module-scope global
      children
        - label Serves stale rows
          desc Loads user 7, the row updates, the next request still gets the pre-update row
        - label Cross-tenant leak
          desc Tenant B sees Tenant A's cached row for the same ID
        - label Cache never reclaimed
          desc Lives for the whole process, not the request
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
